%S A388850 4,8,48,1680,76725,332925,7474752,4541154,75047565,4928180396,
%T A388850 40533366231,111460496439,436502026483,17952448643078
%N A388850 Initial term of first maximal bad interval of width n, i.e., initial term of the first run of exactly n+1 consecutive integers in A388654; or 0 if no such interval exists.
%C A388850 See A388654 for the definition of bad interval.
%C A388850 0 < a(13) <= 17952448643078. (See comment by user StijnC on the Erdős Problems link.)
%C A388850 From _Touch Sungkawichai_, Jan 03 2026: (Start)
%C A388850 0 < a(9) <= 4928180396.
%C A388850 0 < a(10) <= 40533366231.
%C A388850 0 < a(11) <= 111460496439.
%C A388850 0 < a(12) <= 436502026483. (End)
%C A388850 a(15) = 52629641927627, but a(14) is unknown: a(14) = 0 or a(14) > 2*10^14. - _Leandre Jack_, Oct 12 2026
%H A388850 Thomas Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/382">Problem 382</a>, Erdős Problems.
%H A388850 Erdős problems database contributors, <a href="https://github.com/teorth/erdosproblems/blob/main/README.md#table">Erdős problem database</a>, see no. 382.
%H A388850 Leandre Jack, <a href="https://github.com/leandrejack-afk/erdos-computations/blob/main/e382/README.md">Erdős Problem 382: the first maximal bad intervals of widths 9 to 13 and 15</a>, GitHub.
%e A388850 For n = 6, the largest prime factor of the product 7474752*...*7474758 is p = 1367, and the product is divisible by p^2. It is not possible to keep this property if the interval is extended and no earlier interval works (and is maximal), so a(6) = 7474752. (The interval 4541155, ..., 4541161 also works, but is extendable to 4541154, ..., 4541161, giving a(7) = 4541154.)
%Y A388850 Cf. A388654.
%K A388850 nonn,hard,more
%O A388850 0,1
%A A388850 _Pontus von Brömssen_, Sep 21 2025
%E A388850 a(9)-a(13) from _Leandre Jack_, Oct 12 2026
